WEBVTT

00:05.770 --> 00:09.570
Well, it took us a while,
but we finally made it here.

00:10.730 --> 00:13.240
I didn't think that would happen to us.

00:13.570 --> 00:15.490
It's like that "Cow Head" story.

00:15.780 --> 00:20.080
It's your fault, Utsuro.
Running ahead on your own again...

00:21.200 --> 00:22.790
<i>That's why I told you!</i>

00:22.790 --> 00:24.500
<i>Stop being a hotheaded idiot!</i>

00:26.630 --> 00:28.380
Sh-Shut up!

00:28.380 --> 00:29.340
I wanted to...

00:29.340 --> 00:30.630
Wanted to what?

00:32.760 --> 00:34.630
That's enough, rookies.

00:34.800 --> 00:37.340
Looks like we made it here safely.

00:38.300 --> 00:40.510
Our next investigation target.

00:41.350 --> 00:42.520
So this is the place...

00:42.890 --> 00:45.020
Be careful from this point.

00:45.600 --> 00:48.060
We don't know what's hiding where...

00:49.190 --> 00:51.030
Oboro!

00:51.360 --> 00:52.570
Are you okay?

00:57.070 --> 00:58.280
Don't touch me.

00:58.780 --> 01:00.200
I'm fine.

01:00.490 --> 01:02.330
What the hell happened?

01:20.470 --> 01:21.970
I don't know.

01:32.730 --> 01:34.240
URON MIRAGE

02:54.610 --> 02:59.990
URON MIRAGE
CHAPTER 119: THE PHASEY HUNT, PART 4

02:55.440 --> 02:56.780
I don't know.

02:57.030 --> 03:01.110
My blank guard was active.
But it came from behind so quickly...

03:01.110 --> 03:03.280
Damn it, I let my guard down.

03:03.490 --> 03:05.780
Hah, you let me down.

03:05.950 --> 03:07.120
What?

03:07.120 --> 03:11.670
I'm saying that it's not like you
to be so careless on the battlefield!

03:11.790 --> 03:14.420
What did you say?
What the hell do you even know?

03:18.090 --> 03:21.380
Dragon and Tiger, if but steered the wagon,
would be a taiko festival.

03:21.380 --> 03:23.050
That's enough bickering.

03:25.680 --> 03:27.810
It's just as Commander Fuwa had predicted.

03:28.270 --> 03:32.560
The phasey are indeed hiding
inside the run-down building.

03:32.730 --> 03:35.150
What is this place, anyway?

03:35.650 --> 03:38.820
The sign has rotted away
and it's not really legible.

03:38.820 --> 03:42.320
-- RESEARCH FACILITY

03:39.280 --> 03:41.990
Er, nyer... Research Facility.

03:42.530 --> 03:46.660
Seems like it's a facility
that was used to research something.

03:47.200 --> 03:48.620
Let's hurry up and go!

03:48.700 --> 03:51.960
We can't let them escape like they did
in the Recapturing Chaos disaster.

03:52.160 --> 03:53.250
Wait!

03:54.670 --> 03:58.300
Hurried arches of the foot
will not allow for lovingly steamed food.

03:58.420 --> 04:02.720
Young rookies will always panic
and make mistakes. Follow my orders.

04:04.510 --> 04:08.470
I will go east, and Sagiri will go
infiltrate from the west building.

04:08.720 --> 04:11.390
Utsuro and Oboro, you will both wait here.

04:11.390 --> 04:14.350
Wait until one of us calls for backup.

04:14.520 --> 04:18.360
How long are you going
to treat us like novices, Senpai?

04:18.860 --> 04:24.240
We're Feints now, too! So we're
good enough to watch your back.

04:24.740 --> 04:26.160
Oboro.

04:27.370 --> 04:29.370
You're speaking quite a lot today.

04:29.700 --> 04:32.000
Then, I shall teach you one thing.

04:32.410 --> 04:36.500
You know what they say
about chatty lions on the battlefield...

04:37.670 --> 04:39.130
Zack! Behind you!

04:42.800 --> 04:44.130
<i>It is ineffective.</i>

04:45.760 --> 04:47.090
Stand back.

04:48.890 --> 04:51.060
Would you look at that,
Zack's gonna do "that."

04:51.060 --> 04:52.140
"That"?

04:52.140 --> 04:55.900
It's just way too fast,
so no one's really seen it.

04:56.350 --> 04:59.110
Zack Balan's ultimate move!

05:02.360 --> 05:04.150
Oh no, Zack!

05:04.740 --> 05:07.740
What? Zack got eaten!

05:07.740 --> 05:09.910
And he was trying to do something.

05:10.200 --> 05:12.910
It's fine, there's no need to worry.

05:13.120 --> 05:15.790
Then, you're saying Zack is alive?

05:18.080 --> 05:19.670
That's about half true.

05:21.050 --> 05:26.220
It's unclear, but I kind of remember
faintly hearing something about

05:26.220 --> 05:28.840
how phasey crave the power of Feints.

05:28.840 --> 05:35.230
From that, we might be able
to predict with some certainty

05:35.230 --> 05:38.310
that they might want
to absorb Zack's powers.

05:43.110 --> 05:45.820
Oh my, while I was talking...

05:46.240 --> 05:47.820
a whole host of them have arrived!

05:47.820 --> 05:51.490
Sagiri! Were there supposed to be
this many phaseys here?

05:51.490 --> 05:52.830
Who knows?

05:53.200 --> 05:56.460
<i>Damn those old guys.
That trap was a fake.</i>

05:57.160 --> 05:59.790
<i>So that means
they made a decoy look like a bluff.</i>

06:01.630 --> 06:04.460
Utsuro! Oboro!
I'm going to go save Zack.

06:06.130 --> 06:08.180
I'm saying that
I'm leaving this place to you!

06:11.050 --> 06:14.270
Your Body Feints are unknown, right?

06:14.640 --> 06:17.560
Then you'll be able
to easily overcome this challenge!

06:19.940 --> 06:21.060
Yessir!

06:25.440 --> 06:27.440
Don't slow me down.

06:27.610 --> 06:28.820
Back at ya!

06:29.110 --> 06:32.030
They told me to aim for the top,
and that lit a fire in me!

06:38.330 --> 06:41.580
Commander Fuwa,
what do you plan to do?

06:42.500 --> 06:45.630
Honoka, you've grown so much.

06:45.630 --> 06:48.380
It's sexual harassment
to refer to a woman's age.

06:48.380 --> 06:49.800
No.

06:50.680 --> 06:52.220
I meant your measurements.

06:52.220 --> 06:53.930
Have you gone mad?

06:54.810 --> 06:58.850
The Elders will not keep quiet
about your unorthodox methods.

07:04.520 --> 07:05.570
Wait!

07:05.570 --> 07:07.860
We don't want to involve you!

07:07.940 --> 07:10.990
You're off your guard, Teach.

07:11.200 --> 07:12.410
But...

07:12.410 --> 07:14.200
We have no idea

07:14.200 --> 07:16.290
what will happen out there!

07:16.740 --> 07:21.250
Even if you think about it,
the answer is in a grove.

07:23.130 --> 07:26.840
We're going with Sagiri and Zack-senpai!

07:28.840 --> 07:32.640
Commander, do you plan
to initiate a coup?

07:33.550 --> 07:36.310
Or perhaps you're...

07:40.230 --> 07:41.770
It's neither.

07:43.230 --> 07:44.610
But...

07:45.230 --> 07:47.270
it's also both.

07:57.700 --> 07:58.660
No good.

07:58.990 --> 08:03.080
Our cuts are meaningless.
Are phasey immortal?

08:03.290 --> 08:04.790
How should I know?

08:05.250 --> 08:07.290
Don't they have any weaknesses?

08:07.290 --> 08:09.050
Don't ask me!

08:09.260 --> 08:11.800
What's a phasey anyway?

08:12.970 --> 08:15.050
There's something I noticed.

08:15.340 --> 08:18.060
Their movements are too simple.

08:18.180 --> 08:19.850
It's like they're on autopilot.

08:19.850 --> 08:22.810
They're not phaseys, they're phantoms!

08:22.810 --> 08:25.810
They're just puppets who take orders
from the main body.

08:25.980 --> 08:28.270
So only one is real?

08:28.270 --> 08:30.070
No wonder I couldn't cut them down.

08:30.280 --> 08:33.740
Phantoms can only move
according to their orders.

08:33.740 --> 08:35.610
And those orders are probably...

08:35.610 --> 08:37.700
"Attack from behind,"

08:37.870 --> 08:40.950
and "halt your movements when
directly facing a sword wielder."

08:41.200 --> 08:42.160
So, in other words!

08:42.160 --> 08:44.580
Don't show them your back
even if you're surrounded.

08:47.250 --> 08:49.550
Hey, why are you at my six, huh?

08:49.550 --> 08:51.050
Right back at ya.

08:51.210 --> 08:53.840
We'll reveal the main body. Jump!

08:53.840 --> 08:55.590
Don't order me around!

08:58.680 --> 09:00.470
Fleeting Reflection!

09:05.060 --> 09:06.100
There it is!

09:09.570 --> 09:12.400
This time, I'll show you who's stronger.

09:13.360 --> 09:17.360
Who cares? Let that stay uncertain.

09:19.530 --> 09:21.450
Let's go in one go!

09:29.670 --> 09:31.300
Zack!

09:41.890 --> 09:43.430
Let's go in one go!

09:43.720 --> 09:45.430
So this is Uron Mirage?

09:45.600 --> 09:47.100
That's right, Moi!

09:47.100 --> 09:50.190
It's super popular right now,
and Kuku really likes it!

09:50.190 --> 09:53.030
Yeah, but why is, "go in one go"
the signature line?

09:53.030 --> 09:56.700
I'm not really sure,
but it's definitely going in one go!

09:56.700 --> 10:00.200
Those vague and unknown things
are what's making it great!

10:03.040 --> 10:04.700
I don't get it at all.

10:19.510 --> 10:24.270
DIARY OF MY FAVORITE ARTIST

10:23.890 --> 10:27.270
<i>My right hand has white for his coat,
and orange for his hair.</i>

10:27.600 --> 10:31.480
<i>My left hand has navy from his uniform,
and of course red for his scarf.</i>

10:31.900 --> 10:34.280
<i>My favorite character inspired nails
from Uron Mirage.</i>

10:35.730 --> 10:36.490
<i>Wait a second.</i>

10:36.820 --> 10:42.030
<i>They're literally "in my hands."
Utsuro is my right, and Oboro is my left!</i>

10:42.030 --> 10:44.240
<i>I can do anything now.</i>

10:45.580 --> 10:46.950
<i>It makes me want to pray.</i>

10:47.750 --> 10:49.750
<i>Let's upload it to Chitter.</i>

10:49.750 --> 10:52.080
<i>I think I might get a lot of likes from this.</i>

10:52.420 --> 10:55.380
DENGEKI MELON

10:58.010 --> 11:00.090
There's been a lot of tardiness lately.

11:00.090 --> 11:03.300
This time of year might have you feeling
lazy, but please try to stay focused.

11:03.300 --> 11:04.640
Okay, thank you.

11:04.640 --> 11:06.970
Stand. Bow.

11:19.400 --> 11:21.410
Nico, wanna get parfaits?

11:21.410 --> 11:22.320
Yeah!

11:22.490 --> 11:23.530
Yeah!

11:23.530 --> 11:25.580
I don't remember inviting you guys!

11:28.540 --> 11:31.580
And then after that, Oboro said that line!

11:31.670 --> 11:34.000
"They told me to aim for the top,
and that lit a fire in me!"

11:35.920 --> 11:40.300
I thought the scene with Utsuro
and Ms. Honoka was kinda cute.

11:40.510 --> 11:43.760
When he said,
"You're off your guard, Teach."

11:45.510 --> 11:47.060
And then Sagiri's blah blah.

11:47.060 --> 11:48.810
Well, Zack Balan blah blah.

11:48.810 --> 11:54.060
Blah blah blah-blah, blah blahblah.
And then, blah lah, blah. So funny!

11:54.230 --> 11:59.570
Totally blah it. It's bleep-bloop blah blah.
My favorite blerb bler blurh and blah blah!

11:59.740 --> 12:00.610
Blah!

12:00.690 --> 12:01.860
Blah!

12:06.620 --> 12:11.460
<i>Yuri Makuwa, Class 1-3's homeroom teacher,
and Kuku aka Kukumi Ureshino,</i>

12:11.460 --> 12:18.000
<i>are otaku friends who share a love of
the currently airing shonen hit "Uron Mirage."</i>

12:18.460 --> 12:23.260
Yesterday, Haimi... er, you posted
a wonderful illustration.

12:23.470 --> 12:26.970
We got a side-eye glance! I was so excited
I had to cover my mouth.

12:26.970 --> 12:34.650
And this is only my assumption,
but Oboro is slightly... smiling... right?

12:37.650 --> 12:42.150
Haimi, isn't this your first time drawing
Oboro's smile? It's the best thing ever!

12:42.150 --> 12:44.780
And when this week's end card
outed him as a dog person,

12:44.780 --> 12:46.990
I would've understood
if it was Utsuro, but Oboro?

12:46.990 --> 12:49.200
My entire feed was buzzing with excitement.

12:49.200 --> 12:51.830
I also love your color choices, too.

12:51.830 --> 12:55.250
This analogous color scheme
is really great. Oh...

12:55.670 --> 12:57.080
I'm so sorry.

12:57.080 --> 12:59.800
I shouldn't go on about my opinions
in front of the actual person, huh?

12:59.800 --> 13:01.510
No, it makes me happy.

13:03.010 --> 13:05.180
I'm also very happy, too.

13:05.180 --> 13:09.890
You have allowed me to befriend you
when I worshipped you as a god.

13:11.470 --> 13:14.850
Normally I would be prostrating before
you while never making eye contact.

13:14.850 --> 13:17.100
Aww, please get used to it, Ms. Makuwa.

13:17.940 --> 13:22.230
<i>Ureshino and I are the same otaku,
but our stances are strikingly different.</i>

13:22.690 --> 13:28.200
<i>My creed is that, "otaku shall forever
hide in the shadows." However...</i>

13:30.030 --> 13:33.120
<i>even though I became
otaku friends with Ureshino,</i>

13:33.120 --> 13:37.790
<i>I haven't revealed that my Chitter
account name is Dengeki Melon.</i>

13:38.130 --> 13:42.250
<i>I'm still way too embarrassed
to expose my online self to her.</i>

13:42.550 --> 13:46.260
<i>On the other hand, she's enjoying
her hobby to the fullest out in the open.</i>

13:46.260 --> 13:49.760
<i>Even though we're the same otaku, I can
feel the generational gap between us.</i>

13:50.470 --> 13:52.680
<i>We have a student-teacher relationship,</i>

13:52.810 --> 13:56.980
<i>but she's also my dear friend and a godlike
illustrator who draws fantastic art.</i>

13:57.390 --> 14:00.110
<i>I don't want her to be put off by reactions
that are ingrained in my head.</i>

14:00.110 --> 14:02.270
<i>I really don't want my goddess
to hate me.</i>

14:02.860 --> 14:04.240
<i>I need to be careful.</i>

14:04.860 --> 14:07.910
Ms. Makuwa, I actually wanted
to talk to you about something.

14:08.530 --> 14:12.620
I draw illustrations and love it
when people online look at it.

14:12.620 --> 14:15.040
But lately, I've been feeling
like that's not enough.

14:15.040 --> 14:18.290
THEN WHAT THE HELL
WAS THAT THING YESTERDAY?

14:15.290 --> 14:18.290
U.M. has some pretty
unique dialogue, right?

14:18.710 --> 14:23.300
So I'll do my best when drawing, but
it doesn't hold a candle to their one-liners.

14:18.710 --> 14:23.300
IT WAS LIKE A DARK HOT POT PARTY
IN THE GROVE

14:23.550 --> 14:25.130
All right.

14:25.260 --> 14:26.670
<i>Hold on a sec there, Haimi.</i>

14:26.920 --> 14:30.050
So one time, I added a speech bubble
to one of my illustrations,

14:30.050 --> 14:31.720
and filled it in with a phrase.

14:30.050 --> 14:31.720
YOU WOULDN'T LOSE TO A GUY LIKE THAT.

14:31.850 --> 14:35.060
And then my heart couldn't stop racing.

14:35.220 --> 14:37.770
<i>Oh, no. Please, say no more.</i>

14:38.020 --> 14:40.940
<i>If you say what I think
you're going to say, I might faint.</i>

14:41.190 --> 14:45.820
And so... I thought that
I'd like to try it, too.

14:45.820 --> 14:47.570
It's a little embarrassing though.

14:47.860 --> 14:49.950
<i>Please! Don't go any further!</i>

14:50.990 --> 14:52.830
I started drawing manga.

14:56.160 --> 14:58.040
W-Wow.

14:58.660 --> 15:00.920
That's definitely a new challenge for you.

15:02.170 --> 15:03.540
<i>Holy fricking frick, man!</i>

15:03.540 --> 15:05.300
<i>My fave fan artist
is gonna start drawing manga!</i>

15:05.300 --> 15:07.460
<i>Have I died and gone to heaven?
Yay, yay!</i>

15:08.050 --> 15:09.340
<i>O' God.</i>

15:09.630 --> 15:15.350
So, um... It's still a rough draft,
but I brought it with me.

15:18.560 --> 15:20.600
- My eyes! Oh, no!
- Ms. Makuwa?

15:20.810 --> 15:25.440
<i>It's shining! Just like that time Michio Maga
beheld Mr. Tezuka's manga draft!</i>

15:26.070 --> 15:28.150
It's my first time drawing manga,

15:28.150 --> 15:31.490
but I was able to divide the page
into panels like cutting cake.

15:31.660 --> 15:32.820
<i>Is she a genius?</i>

15:32.820 --> 15:36.160
But I can't tell if it's interesting or not.

15:36.450 --> 15:40.120
Ms. Makuwa, you know more about manga
than I do, so can you take a look?

15:49.760 --> 15:54.260
<i>Wow, wow! Haimi's unique touch that
adds cuteness and sexiness to the page.</i>

15:54.260 --> 15:55.970
THANKS TO YOU, I LEARNED
SOMEWHAT OF A NEW SKILL.
THIS ISN'T MUCH, BUT TAKE IT.
IT'S GOOD.
THANKS.

15:54.640 --> 15:57.470
<i>The characters are moving!
And talking!</i>

15:56.220 --> 15:57.770
THAT WAS JUST LUCK.
IT'S NOT LIKE ANYONE WON.
I THINK.
TEEHEE.

15:58.180 --> 16:00.600
<i>Oh! This is...</i>

16:02.060 --> 16:03.520
<i>pretty dang normal.</i>

16:03.810 --> 16:06.650
<i>What? Have I lost my touch?</i>

16:07.480 --> 16:11.860
<i>No, Haimi's distinct, translucent
characteristics have died.</i>

16:12.280 --> 16:15.780
<i>It's fine that the lack of information
makes situations difficult to understand.</i>

16:15.780 --> 16:17.950
<i>However, the panels are divided thinly,</i>

16:17.950 --> 16:20.750
<i>and because the faces are the same size
in every panel, it feels monotonous.</i>

16:20.750 --> 16:24.250
<i>It's difficult to understand the characters'
feelings, which is the most important thing.</i>

16:24.250 --> 16:26.880
<i>Haimi can successfully
capture emotions in her art.</i>

16:26.880 --> 16:30.300
<i>She's already beginning to show that
in her one page illustrations.</i>

16:30.760 --> 16:34.130
<i>The case stems from Haimi
not reading a lot of manga,</i>

16:34.130 --> 16:36.890
<i>so she doesn't quite understand
how to make them.</i>

16:37.640 --> 16:38.890
<i>When it comes to creating worlds
in the 2D medium,</i>

16:38.890 --> 16:42.060
<i>readers are looking for, "the same character
with mutual feelings for loving their world,"</i>

16:42.060 --> 16:44.310
<i>and, "the coincidence of what I was feeling
becomes visualized and verbalized in 2D."</i>

16:44.310 --> 16:46.020
<i>With her extraordinary sense of interpretation
and expressive prowess,</i>

16:46.020 --> 16:47.310
<i>she was fulfilling that at a high level.</i>

16:47.310 --> 16:49.440
<i>But in these small panels,
those abilities aren't shining through.</i>

16:49.440 --> 16:51.820
<i>If you were a veteran otaku woman, then you
can grasp "something" from that outpour.</i>

16:51.820 --> 16:53.280
<i>But these new fans
heavily rely on impressions.</i>

16:53.280 --> 16:55.990
<i>Can we expect newbie otaku who just
became fans to comprehend that?</i>

16:55.990 --> 16:56.620
<i>The answer is no!</i>

16:56.620 --> 16:57.950
<i>Haimi has the talent, the originality,
and a deep passion for the manga.</i>

16:57.950 --> 17:00.040
<i>But the U.M. fandom is full of skilled creators
at the height of their careers.</i>

17:00.040 --> 17:02.290
<i>There aren't many fans with the time
or patience to go hunting for hidden gems!</i>

17:02.290 --> 17:03.160
<i>The current otaku are busy!</i>

17:03.160 --> 17:04.710
<i>At this rate, this small bud that just
came to life will get buried underneath.</i>

17:04.710 --> 17:06.750
<i>If it's not as popular as her illustrations,
she'll think, "Maybe drawing manga isn't for me,"</i>

17:06.750 --> 17:07.960
<i>or, "A person like me should just stick
with one page illustrations forever."</i>

17:07.960 --> 17:08.750
<i>Those are the conclusions
she might come to.</i>

17:08.750 --> 17:10.380
<i>Therefore, the possibility of a number of divine
works being created will be lost forever.</i>

17:10.380 --> 17:11.420
<i>Am I supposed to let that happen?</i>

17:11.420 --> 17:13.590
<i>Hey Dengeki Melon, are you just going to witness
a giant raw gemstone being thrown away?</i>

17:13.590 --> 17:17.800
<i>Could you do something so selfish?
Well, Melon? What's it gonna be?</i>

17:19.310 --> 17:20.390
It was quite fantastic-melon.

17:20.680 --> 17:23.060
Really? Wait, melon?

17:23.270 --> 17:26.230
First, the expressions
on the characters are great.

17:26.230 --> 17:28.810
It really made me think
how amazing manga is.

17:29.020 --> 17:32.440
I do really like it when I can see
my favorite character's face a lot.

17:32.690 --> 17:33.940
<i>I can't go on like this.</i>

17:34.400 --> 17:36.030
The story is really good, too.

17:36.030 --> 17:39.490
They just passed by each other
in front of a vending machine. How exciting.

17:39.490 --> 17:42.790
Utsuro buying a ton of Yobick
was quite endearing, too.

17:42.790 --> 17:46.750
Yes, I knew you'd get it!
I'm so happy!

17:46.750 --> 17:49.540
And then this destructively excellent angle.

17:49.540 --> 17:52.670
A composition where big innocent eyes
are looking down on you, plus that backlight!

17:53.130 --> 17:56.680
I have to applaud you for trying
that idea with Utsuro of all people.

17:58.050 --> 17:59.680
<i>Of course, it's not terrible.</i>

18:00.050 --> 18:02.680
<i>An ordinary person
won't be able to draw this much.</i>

18:03.140 --> 18:07.480
<i>However, if the goal is to convey
Haimi's charms to a large audience,</i>

18:07.480 --> 18:09.560
<i>then there are several points
that need to be addressed.</i>

18:10.440 --> 18:11.940
But I wonder.

18:13.150 --> 18:14.940
Instead of showing it to one amateur,

18:15.070 --> 18:17.530
why don't you ask your online followers?

18:17.530 --> 18:19.280
You have so many of them.

18:19.280 --> 18:20.570
Oh, but...

18:20.910 --> 18:25.080
I think it'll be embarrassing to upload
such a rough draft to the internet.

18:25.290 --> 18:27.000
That's not necessarily true.

18:27.000 --> 18:29.540
I'm sure they'll celebrate
you challenging yourself.

18:29.960 --> 18:33.960
Okay. I guess I'll try uploading it tonight.

18:34.300 --> 18:37.090
It'll probably be better
to hear different opinions.

18:41.760 --> 18:44.430
THIS IS A LITTLE EMBARRASSING, BUT I DREW
A MANGA AND UPLOADED IT.
IT'S JUST A ROUGH DRAFT. H-H-HOW IS IT?

18:42.720 --> 18:45.520
Okay, there. Uploaded.

18:46.100 --> 18:50.810
Ugh, I'm so embarrassed.
What if no one responds to it?

18:50.980 --> 18:55.530
<i>Wait, did I just publish my fantasies
to the entire world?</i>

18:55.780 --> 18:58.610
Isn't that the same
as people seeing you naked?

18:58.820 --> 19:00.360
I gotta delete that post!

19:02.870 --> 19:03.990
What?

19:04.370 --> 19:08.160
Someone already replied.
So fast! Wait, this soon?

19:08.870 --> 19:10.250
Dengeki Melon?

19:10.250 --> 19:13.750
DENGEKI MELON

19:10.750 --> 19:13.750
It's that passionate follower
who always gives me likes.

19:14.460 --> 19:15.750
Whoa, that's thick!

19:16.010 --> 19:19.380
It's such a long reply! What?
They really wrote a lot.

19:19.720 --> 19:22.640
There're no line breaks,
so what they wanted to say is laid on thick!

19:22.720 --> 19:26.020
But they're very polite about it, and
it doesn't make me feel uncomfortable at all.

19:26.220 --> 19:28.270
<i>Each of them are good
constructive criticisms.</i>

19:28.270 --> 19:30.770
It has all the things I wanted to know.

19:30.940 --> 19:34.480
How much manga do you have to read
to get to this level?

19:35.900 --> 19:39.240
Who is this Dengeki Melon person?

19:44.410 --> 19:45.410
Goodness.

19:46.330 --> 19:50.660
So this Dengeki Melon person
really wrote that long of a reply, huh?

19:51.120 --> 19:53.290
<i>My otakuness was overflowing!</i>

19:53.920 --> 19:58.170
Ureshino, do you dislike it when
someone gives their opinion like that?

19:58.510 --> 20:00.010
Of course not.

20:00.010 --> 20:03.340
"They told me to aim for the top,
and that lit a fire in me!"

20:06.010 --> 20:10.640
Dengeki Melon's writing had kindness to it,
while still having a strict point of view.

20:10.640 --> 20:14.900
They also encouraged me to aim
for expressions that'll reach other people.

20:15.360 --> 20:20.070
I came to understand that coming up
with stories isn't my strong suit.

20:20.360 --> 20:22.450
I plan to redraw it from scratch.

20:23.490 --> 20:26.330
So I feel really appreciative.

20:29.160 --> 20:31.460
You're Dengeki Melon, right?

20:32.710 --> 20:35.670
What? H-How did you know?

20:35.960 --> 20:40.460
I went to Dengeki Melon's account
and saw their past comments and posts.

20:40.460 --> 20:42.380
I got curious.

20:42.680 --> 20:45.470
That's when I saw the picture
of the Utsu x Obo nails.

20:45.930 --> 20:48.470
You had the same nails yesterday, right?

20:48.680 --> 20:51.230
Oh. My otakuness was leaking out.

20:51.230 --> 20:53.810
"You're off your guard, Teach."

20:56.360 --> 20:58.520
I don't think you have to hide it.

20:58.980 --> 21:01.780
We're friends who've revealed
everything to each other.

21:02.190 --> 21:04.490
We shouldn't be embarrassed
about anything.

21:04.950 --> 21:06.280
Ureshino.

21:06.450 --> 21:07.490
<i>O' God.</i>

21:07.660 --> 21:11.620
Okay, thank you for taking care
of the story part, Dengeki Melon.

21:13.290 --> 21:15.830
Wait, what? I'm going to write the story?

21:15.830 --> 21:20.840
I really loved that
one short story you posted.

21:21.960 --> 21:23.590
How far back did you go?

21:24.010 --> 21:26.180
That's what I really like.

21:26.180 --> 21:29.600
I like Ms. Makuwa.
And I like Dengeki Melon.

21:29.850 --> 21:32.060
I'm just a plain old otaku though.

21:32.060 --> 21:34.940
There's a side of me
who has fun creating things,

21:35.140 --> 21:37.610
but that short story
was just written on a whim.

21:38.020 --> 21:43.400
But since you've already done it once,
that means you have that passion.

21:44.070 --> 21:45.610
That creative fire.

21:46.570 --> 21:49.490
Oh, please don't say something
so emotional yet perverse.

21:49.740 --> 21:51.990
I will turn your fantasy into a manga!

21:52.120 --> 21:53.120
SHOT TO THE HEART

21:53.500 --> 21:56.870
Plus, we both interpret characters
in the same way.

21:56.870 --> 21:57.880
OH NO

22:03.670 --> 22:05.840
All right, I'll try it.

22:05.840 --> 22:08.840
Hurray! Thank you so much!

22:17.980 --> 22:21.690
<i>Let's celebrate the birth
of a teacher-student manga duo!</i>

22:22.690 --> 22:25.320
We didn't get to do much!

23:57.500 --> 24:01.170
When we complete this mission,
then that secret will finally be revealed.

24:01.170 --> 24:03.540
If that happens, then that
one incident will definitely...

24:03.880 --> 24:06.090
It's that, "You drop three ryou,
pick up a sake bottle."

24:06.090 --> 24:09.510
Next episode on Uron Mirage,
"A Dark, Unknown Shadow Approaches."

24:07.090 --> 24:12.010
NEXT EPISODE
SUMMER DEMON

24:09.510 --> 24:12.010
What will we see beyond the thin mist?
